e-safe Democratic seat into one of the cycle's marquee House contests. Davis has out-raised Buckhout and holds a large cash advantage, while Buckhout benefits from outside-group spending. Recent polls from both partisan sponsors show Davis leading by 8 to 10 points, though earlier surveys were tighter.\n\nExpert ratings are split, with several outlets calling it a Tossup and others leaning toward each party, and prediction markets price Davis's chances in the mid-60s. The race has centered on immigration, gender policy in schools, and Davis's record of rural-health funding and constituent service. Davis holds a modest edge, but the district's new Republican lean keeps the outcome genuinely in doubt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6957, "margin": 2.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6748, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6753, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6783, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6236, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6194, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6727, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6943, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6373, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.6827, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.694, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.6664, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6646, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.5982, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6349, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.63, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6926, "margin": 3.0}]}